# `_docs/` — private, local-only, never in git

**Contract:** `_docs/` is **private planning** (epics, QA CSVs, runbooks, notes). It must **never** appear on GitHub: **do not** `git add` it, **do not** remove it from `.gitignore`, **do not** paste its **contents** (or large excerpts) into issues, PRs, commits, or tracked `.md` files. A **fresh clone has no `_docs/`** — that is normal, not a broken repo.

**Disk:** Git **does not delete** an existing local `_docs/` when you pull, merge, or rewrite remote history. **Never** tell the user to delete `_docs/` to “fix” git. **Never** run `git clean -fdx` without warning — it can remove ignored folders depending on flags.

**Agents:** Use **tracked** docs only (`README.md`, `apps/**/docs/`, `workers/**/README.md`, `.github/`). Root `README.md` has a short human section on this policy.

**What enforces this:** `.gitignore` + this rule + your discipline. **`.cursor/rules/`** only steers Cursor; it cannot retroactively erase past GitHub leaks (history rewrite + force push handles old commits).
